**Remove Duplicates from Array** — Keep unique elements only
______________________________________________________________
import java.util.*;

// Method 1: Using HashSet (fastest)
int[] arr = {1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4};
Set<Integer> unique = new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4));
System.out.println(unique);  // [1, 2, 3, 4]

// Method 2: Preserve order using LinkedHashSet
Set<Integer> ordered = new LinkedHashSet<>(Arrays.asList(1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4));
System.out.println(ordered);  // [1, 2, 3, 4] (in insertion order)

// Method 3: Using Stream API (Java 8+)
List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4);
List<Integer> unique = list.stream().distinct().toList();
System.out.println(unique);  // [1, 2, 3, 4]

